.TH LAMBOOT\-READER 1 "2026-06-03" "lamboot-tools" "lamboot-tools Manual"
.SH NAME
lamboot\-reader \- read and resolve GRUB boot configuration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B lamboot\-reader
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B lamboot\-reader
parses and reasons about GRUB configuration on a Linux host:
.IR grub.cfg ,
.IR /etc/default/grub ,
and
.IR grubenv .
It answers the question "which entry would GRUB boot, with what kernel command
line?" and detects drift between the generated boot menu and the operator
configuration. It is Proxmox\-focused today and best\-effort elsewhere.
.PP
This binary is a prebuilt, statically linked component of the lamboot\-tools
suite, shipped as a standalone CLI. It is also consumed by LamBoot's host\-side
install path and kernel postinst hook to detect command\-line drift and select
the correct kernel for a Boot Loader Specification entry.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list\-kernels
List every menuentry in
.IR grub.cfg .
.TP
.B default
Print the menuentry GRUB would boot right now.
.TP
.B cmdline
Print the effective kernel command line (the resolved default, or a named
kernel version).
.TP
.B compare\-cmdline
Compare the resolved entry's command line against
.IR /etc/default/grub .
Exits 0 on match, 2 on drift.
.TP
.B parse\-default\-grub
Print
.I /etc/default/grub
key/value pairs.
.TP
.B grubenv
Print
.I grubenv
as JSON.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-grub\-cfg " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to
.IR grub.cfg
(default:
.IR /boot/grub/grub.cfg ).
.TP
.BR \-\-default\-grub " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to
.I /etc/default/grub
(default:
.IR /etc/default/grub ).
.TP
.BR \-\-grubenv " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to
.IR grubenv
(default:
.IR /boot/grub/grubenv ).
.TP
.B \-\-json
Machine\-readable JSON output.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print version.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success (for
.BR compare\-cmdline ,
the command line matches).
.TP
.B 2
For
.BR compare\-cmdline ,
configuration drift was detected.
.SH SOURCE
The source for this component lives in its own repository,
.UR https://github.com/lamco-admin/lamboot-reader
.UE .
The binary shipped here is built static against musl for cross\-distribution
portability and vendored into the lamboot\-tools release.
